cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Numbers in Chinese Poetry from the Tang Dynasty Onward"
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-13"
authors:
  - given-names: "Zizheng"
    family-names: "Lv"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-0327-4477"
abstract: >-
  A corpus scan of 175,355 classical Chinese poems from the Tang dynasty through
  the Qing, measuring how often numeral characters appear in shi, ci and qu.
  59.24% of poems contain at least one numeral character; numerals account for
  2.15% of all characters in the corpus. The repository releases the counting
  code, the derived per-collection statistics, and the presentation material
  from which the study originates.
keywords:
